    "body": "## What and why\n\nAttribute the corrected full-donor constructor’s six residual errors from its complete saved journal, without rerunning the model. Five positions have no offered winner; EOS winners fail objective or preservation checks. This determines which proposed explanations the retained evidence supports.\n\n## Result\n\nKEEP saved attribution; model remains REJECTED for promotion. Input is #2069 source4f7eee35, report56faa224; output ce0a6b90. On the original open-development15-position/17-reference/380-guard population, all14,292 alternatives and956 committed epochs are checked. Positions7/8/9/10/13 have zero winning offers. EOS has33:26 CE-only rejections and7 codes of one coordinate vetoed first by the same guard299. None is feasible unselected or later lost. Maximum single feasible offer9/15; accepted whole-answer8/512 unchanged. No model/gradient/score/proposal work or pod.\n\nComplete derived roots and reader/tool evidence are freshly downloaded and verified from iCloud package codex-donor-residual-attribution-20261009 (MD5 96b7e669856a6b0506b70087ce97d529). Next is saved pooled competition/feature-incidence decomposition at earliest residual, before selecting a general learning change. No guard relaxation or answer-specific exception.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Checks at exact head: wording, AST, whitespace, report SHA and normative sealed roots; commands/results posted separately. Rust/model path unchanged; no model retest applicable.\n- [x] Research record: docs/labs/donor-residual-attribution-2026-10-09/README.md\n- [x] New current-state entry with Next\n- [x] Stale-doc search retained; previous prospective question marked completed, historical scope retained\n- [x] STATUS / ROADMAP / #2028 milestone position unchanged (8/512, gate9/15); scoped result goes to M2\n- [x] README headline/capability/mechanism unchanged; no journal entry added\n- [x] Claim-wording gate passes\n- [x] After merge: fresh-main source verification, delete branch/worktree, hygiene, scoped milestone result\n\nReferences #2030\n\n",
